<meta name="description" content="The Securitisation Regulation is a cornerstone of the EU’s efforts to establish a Capital Markets Union. It applies to all securitisation products and includes due diligence, risk retention and transparency rules together with a clear set of criteria to identify simple, transparent and standardised (STS) securitisations." />
